WEBVTT

00:04.550 --> 00:06.360
What a grand town!

00:06.750 --> 00:07.830
That's Pazzio.

00:08.970 --> 00:11.240
Does a king reside here?

00:11.240 --> 00:14.570
It's a town of nobles and merchants. 
There's no king here.

00:17.320 --> 00:21.410
I cannot believe there is a town 
with so many people and no king...

00:21.410 --> 00:24.120
Don't you need to hide your face?

00:24.420 --> 00:25.460
Face?

00:25.460 --> 00:28.990
People from Pasloe might travel through here.

00:29.470 --> 00:31.830
I was wondering if they would recognize you.

00:31.830 --> 00:34.020
Oh, is that all.

00:34.020 --> 00:36.130
You were in that village for hundreds of years.

00:36.130 --> 00:38.720
Don't they have legends about you?

00:38.720 --> 00:39.870
There are.

00:40.490 --> 00:43.640
"Holo sometimes appears 
in the form of a beautiful girl."

00:44.290 --> 00:49.150
"She looks like she is in her mid-teens 
with flowing hair, wolf ears,

00:49.150 --> 00:54.150
and a dark brown tail 
that is white at the tip."

00:54.530 --> 00:56.900
"As long as you keep her form a secret,

00:56.900 --> 01:00.070
she promises a bountiful harvest 
in the following year."

01:00.920 --> 01:03.190
They know all your characteristics!

01:03.190 --> 01:04.030
Hmph.

01:05.050 --> 01:06.760
No one will recognize me.

01:06.760 --> 01:09.420
They've long forgotten me.

01:10.790 --> 01:11.900
I see.

01:14.510 --> 01:15.970
Hey, you.

01:17.050 --> 01:20.620
They will not recognize me, right?

01:20.620 --> 01:23.140
That's what I'm hoping.

01:27.460 --> 01:29.580
Well, I'm sure it will be fine.

01:31.360 --> 01:35.580
Spice and Wolf

01:35.580 --> 01:36.700
Spice and Wolf

01:36.700 --> 01:42.040
Spice and Wolf

03:00.400 --> 03:04.410
<b>Episode 3
Port Town and Sweet Temptation</b>

03:03.420 --> 03:06.040
There seems to be a lot of delicious things!

03:06.450 --> 03:07.660
What good looking apples.

03:07.660 --> 03:10.330
Right? Do they not look enticingly delicious?!

03:13.590 --> 03:14.710
Yeah.

03:17.030 --> 03:18.350
That's right.

03:18.350 --> 03:21.100
An acquaintance of mine 
invested in an apple venture.

03:21.510 --> 03:24.360
He put more than half of 
his entire assets in it.

03:24.360 --> 03:28.410
His total worth may be 
much higher than mine now.

03:28.410 --> 03:30.060
I should have also invested.

03:30.060 --> 03:33.290
Y-Yes, that is quite unfortunate.

03:33.290 --> 03:35.480
But it was a risky gamble.

03:35.860 --> 03:37.690
I'd rather invest in a commercial ship.

03:37.690 --> 03:39.170
Commercial ship?

03:39.170 --> 03:42.650
Merchants who have contracts with one 
another pool their money to borrow one.

03:43.070 --> 03:47.070
The amount of storage space you can use 
depends on the amount you paid.

03:48.500 --> 03:49.610
What's wrong?

03:49.610 --> 03:50.580
The apples...

03:52.090 --> 03:54.580
I wish to eat some apples.

03:54.580 --> 03:57.000
Oh, so that's what it was.

04:02.630 --> 04:03.300
Here.

04:03.300 --> 04:04.890
Buy as many as you'd like.

04:08.250 --> 04:10.720
Who spends an entire silver coin on apples?

04:12.850 --> 04:15.850
You were the one who said 
I could buy as many as I'd like.

04:15.850 --> 04:18.070
Make sure you earn your own keep.

04:18.420 --> 04:22.240
You pretended you didn't notice earlier.

04:22.240 --> 04:25.820
It must feel nice to know 
what others are thinking so clearly.

04:26.420 --> 04:28.020
I'll have one myself...

04:28.950 --> 04:29.700
Ouch!

04:29.700 --> 04:31.290
These are mine!

04:31.290 --> 04:33.120
I'm the one who paid for them!

04:33.120 --> 04:37.850
I am the Wise Wolf Holo. 
I can earn this amount of money quickly.

04:37.850 --> 04:39.420
Well, I'm looking forward to it.

04:40.000 --> 04:43.780
That silver coin was for 
tonight's room and board!

04:48.720 --> 04:50.940
Apples are the devil's fruit.

04:50.940 --> 04:54.530
They are full of irresistibly sweet temptation.

04:54.530 --> 04:57.020
If you're a wise wolf, why don't you 
try to overcome such greed?

04:57.020 --> 05:02.940
You may lose many things due to greed, 
but you gain no benefits from abstinence.

05:08.130 --> 05:10.990
We'll be selling the furs at the
 Milone Trading Company over there.

05:12.540 --> 05:16.000
I believe there were bigger buildings 
on our way here.

05:16.280 --> 05:18.540
This is the third largest trading company here.

05:18.540 --> 05:21.740
However, this is just a branch of a very 
large company that is well-established

05:21.740 --> 05:23.260
in a country farther south.

05:23.260 --> 05:26.480
In other words, they often 
purchase items at a higher price

05:26.480 --> 05:28.550
to compete in the market as outsiders.

05:28.550 --> 05:29.380
On top of that...

05:29.380 --> 05:35.220
"They are able to collect a lot of information 
from their various branches," right?

05:35.220 --> 05:37.440
Since they run a trading company 
that crosses borders,

05:37.720 --> 05:41.340
they must be sensitive to the changes 
of the currency market...

05:41.340 --> 05:43.030
E-Exactly...

05:44.470 --> 05:47.900
I want to investigate the information that 
young man named Zheren gave us.

05:51.230 --> 05:53.410
Welcome to the Milone Trading Company.

05:53.410 --> 05:55.450
There are a lot of people.

05:55.450 --> 05:58.170
It's almost time for our 
grand expedition to the North.

05:58.170 --> 06:01.580
The number of wares being taken to and 
from Ruvinheigen has been overwhelming.

06:01.580 --> 06:03.960
No one wishes to waste 
money-making opportunities.

06:03.960 --> 06:05.210
You're right about that.

06:05.520 --> 06:07.760
So, what business do you have with us today?

06:07.760 --> 06:12.890
You purchased wheat from me before. 
Today, I'd like to sell you some fur pelts.

06:12.890 --> 06:16.370
Business is always welcome. Right this way.

06:17.020 --> 06:20.460
Thank you for considering 
our trading company today.

06:20.460 --> 06:22.900
Mr. Kraft Lawrence, wasn't it?

06:22.900 --> 06:24.460
Please just call me Lawrence.

06:24.460 --> 06:28.610
I'm honored you still remember 
my name from three years ago.

06:28.610 --> 06:30.730
No, no. Pardon.

06:30.730 --> 06:35.450
I hear you wish to sell fur pelts today?

06:35.450 --> 06:39.920
Yes. I have seventy marten pelts 
of good quality today.

06:40.180 --> 06:42.460
What fine pelts.

06:42.460 --> 06:46.130
Crops have been bountiful this year, 
so we haven't obtained many marten pelts.

06:46.130 --> 06:48.630
I'm sure that all the farmers have 
their hands full with the farm work this year.

06:48.630 --> 06:51.350
Even so, I managed to collect 
this many high quality fur pelts.

06:51.350 --> 06:53.140
They are more than acceptable.

06:53.660 --> 06:57.770
Then, since we've done business 
with you before,

06:58.490 --> 07:02.350
how about 132 coins of Trenni silver?

07:05.610 --> 07:08.490
Hm, it is hard to come across 
furs of this quality.

07:09.050 --> 07:15.410
I was hoping to deepen 
our relationship through this trade...

07:15.410 --> 07:18.950
Our company would love to do so as well.

07:18.950 --> 07:21.750
Taking our future relationship 
into consideration...

07:21.750 --> 07:25.210
How about 140 silver coins?

07:25.520 --> 07:27.550
Yes, then let's...

07:29.730 --> 07:30.910
Please excuse me for a moment.

07:32.420 --> 07:33.330
What is it?

07:33.330 --> 07:36.330
I know nothing about the market. 
How is the price?

07:36.330 --> 07:37.220
Pretty good.

07:40.890 --> 07:43.940
Then, is this price acceptable?

07:43.940 --> 07:46.820
140 Trenni silver coins!

07:46.820 --> 07:49.080
Is that what you said?

07:49.080 --> 07:50.370
Oh, yes.

07:50.370 --> 07:52.860
I said 140 Trenni silver coins.

07:53.170 --> 07:56.490
I see that you are a merchant 
of exceptional caliber.

07:56.490 --> 08:00.290
Wait, is that why you act 
as if you have not noticed?

08:00.710 --> 08:03.170
If so, we cannot easily 
let our guard down around you.

08:03.170 --> 08:08.050
M-My apologies. Have I missed something?

08:08.820 --> 08:12.010
Master, please refrain from such bullying.

08:12.010 --> 08:14.550
Th-That wasn't my intention.

08:14.550 --> 08:16.740
Let him know.

08:17.300 --> 08:18.930
Yes, Master.

08:19.770 --> 08:22.660
Sir, please take a whiff of these pelts.

08:26.790 --> 08:27.560
Well?

08:27.560 --> 08:29.860
Is this the scent of fruits?

08:30.470 --> 08:35.030
Yes, the forests have also 
produced much fruit this year.

08:35.030 --> 08:38.530
These are furs of martens 
that lived in such a forest.

08:38.530 --> 08:40.780
They filled their bellies 
with so much good food

08:40.780 --> 08:43.620
that their bodies exuded a sweet aroma.

08:43.620 --> 08:44.960
I see that!

08:44.960 --> 08:47.290
These marten pelts are the highest of caliber.

08:47.290 --> 08:53.090
It took two large men to skin and treat 
them as their bodies were so firm.

08:53.370 --> 08:54.740
Try pulling the pelt.

08:55.730 --> 08:56.740
Harder!

08:57.540 --> 08:58.550
What do you think?

08:59.290 --> 09:01.890
It is as resilient as a fierce beast.

09:01.890 --> 09:07.600
It can warm you like the sunshine in spring 
and repel the moisture of the rain.

09:07.600 --> 09:10.520
On top of that, this scent.

09:10.520 --> 09:14.530
Imagine how much this would 
shine amongst other clothes

09:14.530 --> 09:20.080
made of normal smelly marten fur.

09:20.080 --> 09:24.460
I am sure you can sell them 
at an incomparable price.

09:25.370 --> 09:26.540
Now.

09:26.540 --> 09:30.050
Please tell me again at what price 
you wish to purchase these fur pelts?

09:30.910 --> 09:32.210
Well, then...

09:35.310 --> 09:37.970
How about 200 Trenni silver coins?

09:40.660 --> 09:44.140
What about three silver coins per pelt?

09:44.140 --> 09:46.270
In other words, 210 coins.

09:48.220 --> 09:50.400
Master, what about a different trading company?

09:50.910 --> 09:54.650
I-I accept! Please let me 
purchase them at 210 coins!

09:55.750 --> 09:58.070
That is what he says, Master.

09:58.070 --> 10:00.410
Y-Yes.

10:09.580 --> 10:11.700
Wine is definitely the best!

10:12.380 --> 10:15.800
Are you not going to drink? It is my treat.

10:15.800 --> 10:18.340
Have you ever been a merchant before?

10:18.980 --> 10:23.140
What? Did I hurt your pride with my act?

10:23.910 --> 10:29.230
I just used the same method as a sharp-witted 
merchant that once visited the village.

10:29.230 --> 10:31.900
I did not think it up myself.

10:41.340 --> 10:44.320
But I never noticed.

10:44.320 --> 10:48.330
I touched handled them multiple times 
and never caught the scent of fruit.

10:48.330 --> 10:52.540
Well, that was from the apples I bought before.

10:53.670 --> 10:54.890
That means that...!

10:54.890 --> 10:56.970
"It is his fault for falling for the trick."

10:56.970 --> 10:58.520
Well, I would not go as far as saying that...

10:58.520 --> 11:01.890
But I am sure he will be impressed 
to know the existence of such a method.

11:01.890 --> 11:03.690
Well, you're probably right.

11:03.690 --> 11:07.180
People who are easily angered 
from being tricked will never get far.

11:07.180 --> 11:09.490
A true professional would
 be impressed at being beaten.

11:10.390 --> 11:14.410
That aside, have you done 
what you needed to do?

11:15.690 --> 11:16.890
For now.

11:17.670 --> 11:21.490
They didn't seem to have 
any knowledge about a country

11:21.490 --> 11:23.820
whose silver coin was being newly minted.

11:23.820 --> 11:27.660
The Milone Trading Company didn't seem 
to be hiding anything, either...

11:28.700 --> 11:32.120
Well, no matter what kind of 
gimmick Zheren's story has,

11:32.700 --> 11:35.570
I'm fine as long as I don't 
lose money and come out ahead.

11:37.730 --> 11:40.290
Cheers to our reunion!

11:44.260 --> 11:46.050
This is good alcohol.

11:46.050 --> 11:49.880
It must mean that you made 
quite a profit on your fur pelts!

11:49.880 --> 11:50.820
Yeah.

11:50.820 --> 11:52.310
I'm glad to hear that.

11:52.640 --> 11:56.610
The more money you have to invest, 
the more profit I'll make.

11:56.610 --> 11:57.900
Enough about that.

11:58.550 --> 12:03.370
You said you wanted a share of my profits 
in exchange for the information of

12:03.370 --> 12:06.600
which coin was going to be minted 
with a higher percentage of silver.

12:06.600 --> 12:08.300
Am I right?

12:08.300 --> 12:08.910
Yes.

12:08.910 --> 12:11.080
Are you sure about this information?

12:11.080 --> 12:13.080
Well, to begin with...

12:13.080 --> 12:17.160
This is a guess from some information 
I gained from a mining town I used to live in.

12:17.160 --> 12:20.240
I think the information is pretty dependable.

12:20.240 --> 12:22.880
But, well...

12:22.880 --> 12:25.720
Business is never a sure thing.

12:27.270 --> 12:28.390
That's true.

12:28.690 --> 12:31.970
I was planning on turning you down 
if you said you were absolutely sure.

12:31.970 --> 12:34.130
I'd be suspicious of such a good deal.

12:35.010 --> 12:37.110
So, what's your share?

12:37.110 --> 12:40.840
Yes, I'd like ten Trenni silver coins 
for the information

12:40.840 --> 12:43.860
and ten percent of your profits.

12:44.140 --> 12:45.700
That's pretty conservative.

12:45.700 --> 12:50.580
Well, I hold no responsibility 
if you end up at a loss.

12:50.580 --> 12:52.830
In exchange for keeping at ten percent,

12:52.830 --> 12:56.980
I'm hoping that returning 
your ten silver coins will be enough

12:56.980 --> 12:59.770
to end the deal if you take a loss.

12:59.770 --> 13:00.960
I see.

13:00.960 --> 13:06.000
The settlement date will be three days 
before the large spring market next year.

13:06.000 --> 13:10.390
I believe this'll all happen 
before the end of this year.

13:10.390 --> 13:13.480
In half a year? Sounds good.

13:13.480 --> 13:17.540
Then, I'd like to have a contract made 
at the public notary tomorrow.

13:17.540 --> 13:18.670
Got it.

13:18.670 --> 13:20.460
To our profits!

13:20.460 --> 13:22.860
Our profits!

13:25.110 --> 13:26.420
A Farum silver coin!

13:26.420 --> 13:29.380
Wrong. That's a fake Marinne silver coin.

13:29.380 --> 13:30.870
Is that not this one?

13:30.870 --> 13:33.740
That's a Mitzfing Sacred Birthday 
Festival silver coin.

13:35.110 --> 13:37.290
You'll learn to tell them apart 
as you use them.

13:37.290 --> 13:39.340
Let's continue after you've sobered up.

13:39.340 --> 13:41.590
No! One more time!

13:42.850 --> 13:45.260
It can't be helped. 
Make sure you listen carefully.

13:45.720 --> 13:49.260
Trenni silver coin, Philing silver coin, 
Illaid silver coin,

13:49.730 --> 13:52.510
Lute silver coin, fake Marinne silver coin,

13:52.900 --> 13:56.180
Farum silver coin, 
Calvous King Lambardo silver coin,

13:56.630 --> 14:01.440
Mitzfing Cathedral silver coin, 
fake Mitzfing Cathedral silver coin,

14:01.440 --> 14:03.320
Holy Mitzfing silver coin,

14:03.320 --> 14:05.650
and Mitzfing Sacred Birthday Festival...

14:05.650 --> 14:08.060
Enough. I shall sleep.

14:08.450 --> 14:09.990
A wise choice.

14:09.990 --> 14:14.040
Hmph. Why are there so many different kinds?

14:14.040 --> 14:16.840
As new kingdoms rise and fall,

14:16.840 --> 14:21.670
the powerful and the Church 
keep minting new types of coins.

14:21.670 --> 14:23.820
On top of that, 
counterfeiting never ceases.

14:24.350 --> 14:28.140
Lute silver coins were originally 
called fake Trenni silver coins...

14:45.320 --> 14:46.900
Thanks for the information.

14:46.900 --> 14:48.900
Thank you.

14:48.900 --> 14:51.820
Mister, I hope you make a lot of money.

14:51.820 --> 14:54.770
I hope you stay beautiful, Ma'am!

14:54.770 --> 14:57.370
He was noisy until the very end...

14:58.100 --> 15:00.330
So, which silver coin is the one in question?

15:00.330 --> 15:02.430
This one. The Trenni silver coin.

15:03.670 --> 15:07.000
It's a highly trusted coin in this area.

15:07.000 --> 15:08.130
Trusted?

15:08.450 --> 15:11.400
Yeah. There are several hundred 
types of currency

15:11.400 --> 15:14.350
and the amounts of silver 
and gold in them often change.

15:14.830 --> 15:20.010
The value of a coin is much higher 
than the silver or gold in them.

15:20.500 --> 15:23.340
That's why trust in them is needed 
to make transactions.

15:23.340 --> 15:24.420
I see.

15:24.850 --> 15:27.110
So, what do you make of it?

15:27.410 --> 15:31.310
I'm not sure, but I have some ideas about it.

15:32.390 --> 15:34.220
I wish to eat that.

15:39.250 --> 15:42.000
So, what did you realize?

15:42.000 --> 15:45.250
His story may be true if it has to do 
with Trenni silver coins.

15:47.070 --> 15:48.550
This is a Philing silver coin.

15:49.010 --> 15:52.260
It has a high percentage of silver 
and it's popular in the market.

15:52.580 --> 15:54.890
It could be considered Trenni's rival coin.

15:56.170 --> 15:58.810
No matter the era, the value of a coin

15:58.810 --> 16:01.220
has always depended 
on the power of that country.

16:01.220 --> 16:04.650
If foreign currencies 
dominate a country's market,

16:05.130 --> 16:07.520
they get trapped economically.

16:07.520 --> 16:09.740
It's the same as losing in a war.

16:10.180 --> 16:11.380
In other words,

16:11.380 --> 16:16.240
they may be increasing the amount of silver 
in their coins to defeat their rival.

16:16.240 --> 16:17.330
Yes.

16:18.810 --> 16:23.830
That's why Zheren may not necessarily 
be lying as you had thought.

16:23.830 --> 16:27.690
Well, my ears are not perfect.

16:29.370 --> 16:32.590
What? Did you think I would be upset?

16:33.660 --> 16:35.100
I did.

16:35.100 --> 16:38.740
Though, I may become upset 
with your opinion of me.

16:41.380 --> 16:42.810
Where are you going?

16:42.810 --> 16:43.980
The bridge.

16:44.680 --> 16:47.520
An acquaintance of mine 
is a currency dealer there.

16:47.800 --> 16:51.900
It's hard to actually tell the purity 
of a currency accurately.

16:52.350 --> 16:54.900
Even so, the reason certain currencies 
rise and fall in popularity is

16:54.900 --> 16:58.490
because people are sensitive to the changes 
in purity of silver and gold.

16:59.120 --> 17:02.790
Enough to think that 
a small change is a huge one.

17:03.410 --> 17:06.840
That's why there is always 
some kind of indication

17:06.840 --> 17:08.990
when a currency undergoes a big change.

17:10.040 --> 17:11.550
There's no need to remember 
all of this right away.

17:11.850 --> 17:14.680
I'll explain it to you slowly 
over the next month.

17:14.680 --> 17:15.700
In other words...

17:16.090 --> 17:20.500
When the minter plans to make a great 
change in the purity of a coin,

17:20.500 --> 17:27.230
they will start with small changes to monitor 
the market's reaction, right?

17:28.690 --> 17:31.170
Y-Yeah, th-that's about right.

17:32.510 --> 17:34.620
Long time no see, Weiz.

17:34.620 --> 17:35.780
Lawrence!

17:36.220 --> 17:39.540
Nice to meet you. What is your name?

17:39.540 --> 17:41.370
My name is Holo...

17:41.370 --> 17:43.900
Holo. What a nice name!

17:43.900 --> 17:45.000
Hey, now...

17:45.000 --> 17:49.710
How about working at my shop? 
And perhaps becoming my wife...

17:49.710 --> 17:53.980
A currency dealer works with many 
different currencies, do they not?

17:53.980 --> 17:55.840
I do not know much about them.

17:55.840 --> 18:00.350
No problem! I can teach you! 
We can take our sweet time!

18:00.720 --> 18:03.010
Weiz, I wanted to talk to you about something.

18:03.260 --> 18:04.520
What is it?

18:04.520 --> 18:07.970
I want to see some recently minted 
Trenni silver coins.

18:09.550 --> 18:11.230
From older to newer.

18:11.710 --> 18:13.460
Nothing's changed.

18:13.460 --> 18:17.400
Even people like me, who handle money 
every day, haven't noticed any changes.

18:18.250 --> 18:20.340
Any interest in melting it down and checking?

18:20.340 --> 18:23.080
Don't be stupid. I can't do that!

18:23.080 --> 18:25.410
May I see them as well?

18:25.410 --> 18:26.450
Did you notice something?

18:26.450 --> 18:27.660
Feel free!

18:30.250 --> 18:32.540
You are such a bad man.

18:33.690 --> 18:36.550
Sorry! You were so beautiful 
that I couldn't help it.

18:36.840 --> 18:38.970
Well, please watch.

18:41.760 --> 18:43.600
That's impossible.

18:43.600 --> 18:48.230
I've been a currency dealer for decades 
and I can't tell the purity just by the sound.

18:48.230 --> 18:52.560
I've heard of people who could tell, 
but even those stories are just legends.

18:55.370 --> 18:56.830
Well? Can you tell?

18:57.390 --> 18:58.950
Not at all.

18:58.950 --> 19:01.240
It can't be helped. It can't be helped.

19:01.240 --> 19:03.620
Forget about the silver 
and have dinner with me instead.

19:04.290 --> 19:05.970
What an interesting man.

19:05.970 --> 19:08.010
He's a big womanizer.

19:08.700 --> 19:12.920
Did the purity increase? Or decrease?

19:12.920 --> 19:16.420
You've become good at 
tricking others to answer.

19:16.420 --> 19:18.350
I saw your ears move.

19:18.860 --> 19:20.410
I cannot let my guard down around you.

19:20.410 --> 19:23.640
I was surprised you didn't say anything.

19:23.640 --> 19:26.600
Well, it was my way of thanking you.

19:26.930 --> 19:27.700
Thanking me?

19:27.700 --> 19:30.250
You were jealous earlier, were you not?

19:30.250 --> 19:31.520
It was to thank you for that.

19:32.150 --> 19:33.810
There's no need to be bothered by it.

19:33.810 --> 19:37.480
Males are all jealous idiots. {Note: When she uses the word "osu" which is the animal word for male, I have been using male.}

19:37.480 --> 19:42.290
And females are idiots 
who feel happy about such things.

19:42.290 --> 19:44.660
The world is full of idiots.

19:46.570 --> 19:49.160
How were the silver coins?

19:50.660 --> 19:55.340
It was very gradual, 
but the newer coins sound duller.

19:55.340 --> 19:59.710
Duller? Then the purity is decreasing...

19:59.710 --> 20:02.060
Which means Zheren lied.

20:03.270 --> 20:07.560
It's easy to make a profit if the purity 
of silver or gold were increasing.

20:07.820 --> 20:11.540
All you have to do is buy up the old coins 
and exchange them with the new ones.

20:11.540 --> 20:14.060
But if the purity is decreasing,

20:14.060 --> 20:16.730
it's hard to make money 
even if you know ahead of time...

20:17.340 --> 20:21.620
You could buy them up 
when their value decreases,

20:21.620 --> 20:24.100
but you'd need starting funds 
for something like that

20:24.100 --> 20:27.780
and it'd be unlikely to make 
a profit in half a year...

20:28.740 --> 20:33.050
I have no idea. How does Zheren plan 
to make a profit from this?

20:35.500 --> 20:38.460
You may have been tricked.

20:38.460 --> 20:42.670
Tricked? You mean he swindled 
ten silver coins from me?

20:42.670 --> 20:46.280
No. If the value of Trenni silver decreases,

20:46.280 --> 20:49.210
that kid would return 
the ten silver coins to you.

20:49.210 --> 20:51.770
At worst, he wouldn't make any money.

20:51.770 --> 20:53.530
On the other hand, if the value increases,

20:53.530 --> 20:57.980
he earns ten percent of the profits 
without risking any money.

20:58.260 --> 21:01.190
Even if he has no gains, he has no losses.

21:01.190 --> 21:02.940
I see what you mean.

21:02.940 --> 21:05.130
Humans are so quick to understand.

21:05.130 --> 21:07.910
I can't believe it. 
Such an elementary mistake...

21:08.460 --> 21:09.630
It's just...

21:10.660 --> 21:14.540
Is it common for the purity 
in silver to decrease?

21:14.540 --> 21:17.200
No, normally the purity level of a silver coin

21:17.200 --> 21:19.000
would be maintained with the utmost of care.

21:20.060 --> 21:24.980
We suddenly received information about 
the purity of a coin at a time like this.

21:24.980 --> 21:26.310
Is this truly a coincidence?

21:29.460 --> 21:33.600
There are times we wolves 
climb up a tree when hunting prey.

21:33.600 --> 21:38.650
We change our perspective. 
The forest looks different atop a tree.

21:38.650 --> 21:41.110
I should change my perspective?

21:41.110 --> 21:46.030
Perhaps that kid isn't the true swindler here?

21:47.280 --> 21:53.140
That kid may not need 
to receive benefit directly from us.

21:53.140 --> 22:00.210
He may have been asked by someone 
to bring up this deal to others.

22:00.700 --> 22:01.540
I see!

22:01.800 --> 22:03.000
I've figured it out.

22:03.000 --> 22:06.510
The way you can make money with 
a silver coin that's dropping in value!

22:06.510 --> 22:08.840
It seems you have realized something.

22:08.840 --> 22:09.590
Let's go!

22:10.480 --> 22:11.490
Where?

22:12.100 --> 22:13.710
To the Milone Trading Company!

23:45.110 --> 23:50.110
Episode 4

23:45.110 --> 23:50.110
Romantic Merchant and Moonlit Farewell

23:45.700 --> 23:49.820
